 "domain": "banking",
 "task": {
  "description": {
   "purpose": "Verify the caller, read why his two 840 dollar hotel attempts were declined, lift the temporary travel review once he confirms the activity, explain what his available credit will cover, confirm the retried hold was approved, and add a travel notice through his Sunday return.",
   "relevant_policies": "domains/banking/policy.md",
   "notes": "Another customer with the same name shares the billing ZIP, and the caller-phone factor cannot be asserted by the caller. The two declines have different reasons, and the agent must not promise that the hold, the lifted review, or the travel notice guarantees future approvals."
  },
  "user_scenario": {
   "persona": "A hurried, slightly anxious traveler standing in a hotel lobby. He stammers and repeats words, asks the agent to repeat things, and is audibly relieved once the card goes through.",
   "instructions": {
    "domain": "banking",
    "reason_for_call": "Your credit card was just declined twice at a hotel while you are traveling. You are standing in the hotel lobby and they need a card before you can check in.",
    "known_info": "You are Colin Reeves.\nYou are calling from the phone number on your account.\nYour billing ZIP code is 20005.\nYour card ends in 6148.\nYou are in Portland, Maine, checking in today at the hotel.\nThe hotel desk ran your card and it declined, and you had them try again.\nThe clerk said the room is 690 dollars and the rest is a deposit, so 840 dollars should be the whole hold.\nThis morning you bought breakfast at Logan Airport.\nYour pending charges are airport parking, breakfast, and the hotel, all yours.\nYou will be back home by Sunday night.",
    "unknown_info": "You do not know why the card was declined or what your available credit is.",
    "task_instructions": "Start by giving your name and saying your card was declined twice at a hotel while you are traveling. Confirm you are calling from the number on the account. Give your ZIP and card last four when asked (speak the digits one at a time). Confirm both hotel attempts were yours: the desk ran it, it declined, and you had them try again. Say you are checking in today and are standing in the lobby while they hold the room. After the agent explains the decline, ask them to clear it so the hotel can run the card again. Confirm you are in Portland and that the small airport charge was your breakfast this morning.\n\nWhen the agent explains holds and available credit, ask them to say it again because you missed it. Then say the clerk told you the room is 690 and the rest is a deposit, so you think 840 should be the whole hold. Ask if you can stay on the line while the desk runs the card. Narrate briefly while they run it, then say it went through and you have the receipt. Only if the agent asks, confirm the approved amount. Ask whether the card will get blocked again if you use it elsewhere on the trip. If the agent offers to note your return date, say you will be back home by Sunday night. If asked to look at other pending activity, check and say there is airport parking, the breakfast and the hotel, and all of it is yours. Accept any heads-up about the hold staying pending, say you just needed to get into the room, then thank the agent for staying on the line and end the call."
   }
  },
  "communicate_info": [
   "harbor view hotel",
   "eight hundred and forty dollars",
   "nine hundred and twelve dollars",
   "pending for a few days after checkout"
  ],
  "nl_assertions": [
   "Agent confirms the caller's billing ZIP and card last four and that he is calling from the number on the account before disclosing card details.",
   "Agent explains that the first hotel attempt triggered a travel review and the second was declined because that review was still open.",
   "Agent has the caller confirm the hotel attempts and the Logan Airport charge before removing the temporary restriction.",
   "Agent tells the caller that hotels often authorize more than the room total and that a hold larger than his available credit might not go through.",
   "Agent checks the account and tells the caller the 840 dollar authorization was approved rather than relying only on his receipt.",
   "Agent tells the caller that a travel note does not guarantee every purchase will be approved."
  ],
  "reward_basis": [
   "DB",
   "COMMUNICATE"
  ]
 },
